        mech1 = "Why does BOILING remove temporary hardness Ca(HCO₃)₂ but fail on permanent CaSO₄? Heating decomposes soluble bicarbonate Ca(HCO₃)₂(aq) → insoluble CaCO₃(s) kettle scale + CO₂ + H₂O, stripping Ca²⁺ out of solution—whereas CaSO₄ stays heat-stable until Washing Soda Na₂CO₃ swaps Ca²⁺ into insoluble CaCO₃!",
